The Wizard is high-level enough to evade wands of death
fairly frequently.  Melee-strong characters (Barbarians,
Valkyries, Knights, Samurai, and some Tourists; not sure
about Rogues, as I've not palyed them much) can often kill
him faster that way.  Rangers can and should turn him into
a pincushion; Samurai can do that as well, if they've
chosen to develop the bow skill.  As a Monk, however, you
may want to consider other options.

Wands, as I understand it, don't benefit from your
character's (presumably high at this point) experience
level in the way that spells do, so he may be less able to
dodge if you *cast* something at him, rather than using a
wand.  I haven't worked out the numbers for this, though,
and I haven't got a monk that far into the game yet, so
I suppose I could be wrong.

